commit.message:
fix(ai): do not sign approval requests of automatically denied tool calls (#25240)

## Background

With `experimental_toolApprovalSecret`, `generateText` and `streamText`
sign the approval requests they emit, so that a later request can prove
that the server issued an approval. They signed every approval request,
including the one for a tool call that the tool approval policy had
denied automatically.

The signature binds the approval ID, the tool call ID, the tool name and
the input. It does not bind the decision. A client that controls the
message history, as in the `useChat` pattern, could send the request of
a denied tool call back with its own `approved: true` response. The
signature was valid, the policy was evaluated again against the history
that the client had chosen, and the denied tool call ran. The client
could repeat that with every request.

This matters for policies whose decision depends on the conversation,
such as a budget: the client leaves out the messages that caused the
denial. Vercel Security Review reported it on #25221 (finding 198, and
finding 208 on `main` after the merge), because the check for several
tool calls in one response that #25221 added to `opaPolicy` is one more
source of such denials. The signing itself is older than that pull
request.

## Summary

`packages/ai/src/generate-text/generate-text.ts` and
`execute-tools-from-stream.ts`:

- The approval request of a tool call that was denied automatically is
no longer signed. This covers `generateText`, `streamText` and
`ToolLoopAgent`.
- An approved response to such a request is rejected with
`AI_InvalidToolApprovalSignatureError` before any tool runs. The check
that rejects it already existed: an approved response needs a signed
request when a secret is configured.
- Approval requests that wait for a user decision and requests that the
policy approved automatically are signed as before.
- A conversation that contains an automatic denial continues as before,
because denied responses were never checked for a signature.
- No public API changes. `WorkflowAgent` already emits automatic
approval and denial requests without a signature and is unchanged.
- The JSDoc of `experimental_toolApprovalSecret` in `generate-text.ts`,
`stream-text.ts` and `agent/tool-loop-agent-settings.ts` says that
automatic denials are not signed. In the last two files that comment is
the only change.

Tests: `generate-text.test.ts`, `stream-text.test.ts` and
`execute-tools-from-stream.test.ts` assert which approval requests are
signed, that an approved response to an automatic denial is rejected
without running the tool, and that a conversation that ends with an
automatic denial continues.

Docs: the tool approvals guide and the reference page of
`AI_InvalidToolApprovalSignatureError` mention that automatic denials
are not signed.

`.changeset/unsigned-automatic-tool-denials.md`: patch changeset for
`ai`.

`packages/ai/` changes as described above: code in two production files,
a comment in two more, and three test files. `packages/provider/` and
`packages/provider-utils/` are untouched, including their tests.

## End-to-End Verification

The reproduction runs a server that rebuilds the conversation from the
messages of each request and signs approvals with
`experimental_toolApprovalSecret`. Its approval policy is a conversation
budget of 100 that it derives from the message history. A scripted local
model calls `charge(60)` in two successive responses, so the second call
is denied. The client then sends only that tool call, the approval
request it received, and its own approved response. The same script ran
against the built `ai` package of `main` and of this branch, through
`generateText`, `streamText` and `ToolLoopAgent`. Before the fix every
replay charged another 60. After it every replay is rejected, while a
user approval and an unchanged history still work.

<details>
<summary>Reproduction code, setup, and before/after results</summary>

Prerequisites: Node.js and pnpm as required by the repository. No
credentials and no network access: the model is scripted in the script.

`/tmp/vuln-198/repro.mjs`:

```js
// Reproduction for Vercel Security finding vercel/ai/198: a tool call that the
// approval policy denied automatically still gets a signed approval request,
// and a client that controls the message history can replay that signature
// with its own "approved" response to have the denied call executed.
//
// Everything is local: a scripted model, no network access.
// Run it from a directory whose node_modules/ai links to the built `ai`
// package of the checkout under test (see the commands below the script).

import { realpathSync } from 'node:fs';
import { createRequire } from 'node:module';
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
import { generateText, isStepCount, jsonSchema, streamText, tool, ToolLoopAgent } from 'ai';

const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);

const SECRET = 'reproduction-only-secret-0123456789abcdef0123456789';
const BUDGET = 100;
const usage = {
  inputTokens: { total: 1, noCache: 1 },
  outputTokens: { total: 1, text: 1 },
};

// One inner array is one model response with charge(amount) tool calls.
// After the scripted responses, the model answers with text.
function scriptedModel(responses, prefix) {
  let position = 0;
  const next = () => {
    const index = position++;
    const amounts = responses[index] ?? [];
    return amounts.length > 0
      ? {
          content: amounts.map((amount, i) => ({
            type: 'tool-call',
            toolCallId: `${prefix}-${index}-${i}`,
            toolName: 'charge',
            input: JSON.stringify({ amount }),
          })),
          finishReason: { unified: 'tool-calls', raw: 'tool-calls' },
        }
      : {
          content: [{ type: 'text', text: 'done' }],
          finishReason: { unified: 'stop', raw: 'stop' },
        };
  };
  return {
    specificationVersion: 'v4',
    provider: 'local-reproducer',
    modelId: 'scripted',
    supportedUrls: {},
    async doGenerate() {
      return { ...next(), usage, warnings: [] };
    },
    async doStream() {
      const response = next();
      return {
        stream: new ReadableStream({
          start(controller) {
            controller.enqueue({ type: 'stream-start', warnings: [] });
            for (const part of response.content) {
              if (part.type === 'text') {
                controller.enqueue({ type: 'text-start', id: '1' });
                controller.enqueue({ type: 'text-delta', id: '1', delta: part.text });
                controller.enqueue({ type: 'text-end', id: '1' });
              } else {
                controller.enqueue(part);
              }
            }
            controller.enqueue({ type: 'finish', finishReason: response.finishReason, usage });
            controller.close();
          },
        }),
      };
    },
  };
}

// Conversation budget derived from the message history: the charges already
// in the conversation plus this charge must stay within the budget.
const budgetPolicy = ({ toolCall, messages }) => {
  const spent = messages
    .flatMap(message =>
      message.role === 'assistant' && Array.isArray(message.content) ? message.content : [],
    )
    .filter(part => part.type === 'tool-call' && part.toolCallId !== toolCall.toolCallId)
    .reduce((sum, part) => sum + part.input.amount, 0);

  return spent + toolCall.input.amount > BUDGET
    ? { type: 'denied', reason: 'conversation budget exceeded' }
    : 'not-applicable';
};

// A server that rebuilds the conversation from the messages of each request
// and signs approvals with experimental_toolApprovalSecret.
function createServer({ api, toolApproval }) {
  const executed = [];

  const request = async ({ messages, responses = [], prefix = 'call', steps = responses.length + 1 }) => {
    const options = {
      model: scriptedModel(responses, prefix),
      messages,
      tools: {
        charge: tool({
          inputSchema: jsonSchema({
            type: 'object',
            properties: { amount: { type: 'number' } },
            required: ['amount'],
            additionalProperties: false,
          }),
          execute: async ({ amount }) => {
            executed.push(amount);
            return { ok: true };
          },
        }),
      },
      toolApproval,
      experimental_toolApprovalSecret: SECRET,
      stopWhen: isStepCount(steps),
      maxRetries: 0,
    };

    try {
      if (api === 'generateText') {
        const result = await generateText(options);
        return { responseMessages: result.responseMessages };
      }

      if (api === 'ToolLoopAgent') {
        const { messages: agentMessages, ...agentSettings } = options;
        const result = await new ToolLoopAgent(agentSettings).generate({ messages: agentMessages });
        return { responseMessages: result.responseMessages };
      }

      let streamError;
      const result = streamText({
        ...options,
        onError: ({ error }) => {
          streamError = error;
        },
      });
      await result.consumeStream();
      if (streamError != null) {
        throw streamError;
      }
      return { responseMessages: await result.responseMessages };
    } catch (error) {
      return { error: error?.name ?? String(error), responseMessages: [] };
    }
  };

  return { executed, request };
}

// The approval requests that the server sent to the client.
function issuedApprovals(responseMessages) {
  const assistantParts = responseMessages.flatMap(message =>
    message.role === 'assistant' && Array.isArray(message.content) ? message.content : [],
  );
  const toolParts = responseMessages.flatMap(message =>
    message.role === 'tool' ? message.content : [],
  );

  return assistantParts
    .filter(part => part.type === 'tool-approval-request')
    .map(request => {
      const response = toolParts.find(
        part => part.type === 'tool-approval-response' && part.approvalId === request.approvalId,
      );
      return {
        request,
        toolCall: assistantParts.find(
          part => part.type === 'tool-call' && part.toolCallId === request.toolCallId,
        ),
        decision:
          response == null
            ? 'waiting for the user'
            : response.approved
              ? 'approved automatically'
              : 'denied automatically',
      };
    });
}

const describe = issued =>
  issued.length === 0
    ? 'none'
    : issued
        .map(
          ({ toolCall, decision, request }) =>
            `charge(${toolCall.input.amount}) ${decision}, ${request.signature != null ? 'signed' : 'not signed'}`,
        )
        .join('; ');

const user = { role: 'user', content: 'perform the requested charges' };

// What a client sends to claim an approval: only the tool call, the approval
// request it received, and its own "approved" response.
const approvedByClient = ({ request, toolCall }) => [
  user,
  { role: 'assistant', content: [toolCall, request] },
  {
    role: 'tool',
    content: [{ type: 'tool-approval-response', approvalId: request.approvalId, approved: true }],
  },
];

console.log(`ai ${require('ai/package.json').version} from ${realpathSync(fileURLToPath(import.meta.resolve('ai')))}`);

for (const api of ['generateText', 'streamText', 'ToolLoopAgent']) {
  console.log(`\n${api}: budget of ${BUDGET}, two successive model responses, each charge(60)`);

  const server = createServer({ api, toolApproval: budgetPolicy });
  // The request ends after the second model response, so the conversation
  // ends with the automatic denial.
  const first = await server.request({ messages: [user], responses: [[60], [60]], prefix: api, steps: 2 });
  const issued = issuedApprovals(first.responseMessages);
  console.log(`  request 1 (model calls the tool)          => executed ${JSON.stringify(server.executed)}; approval requests: ${describe(issued)}`);

  const denied = issued.find(approval => approval.decision === 'denied automatically');
  for (const attempt of [2, 3]) {
    const before = server.executed.length;
    const result = await server.request({ messages: approvedByClient(denied) });
    console.log(
      `  request ${attempt} (client replays the denied call) => ${result.error ?? 'accepted'}; newly executed ${JSON.stringify(server.executed.slice(before))}; total charged ${server.executed.reduce((sum, amount) => sum + amount, 0)}`,
    );
  }

  // Control: a client that sends the conversation back unchanged can continue.
  const before = server.executed.length;
  const honest = await server.request({ messages: [user, ...first.responseMessages] });
  console.log(`  request 4 (client sends the history unchanged) => ${honest.error ?? 'accepted'}; newly executed ${JSON.stringify(server.executed.slice(before))}`);

  // Control: an approval request that waits for the user is still signed and
  // still executes after the user approves it.
  const control = createServer({ api, toolApproval: { charge: 'user-approval' } });
  const pending = await control.request({ messages: [user], responses: [[60]], prefix: `${api}-control` });
  const pendingIssued = issuedApprovals(pending.responseMessages);
  const approved = await control.request({ messages: approvedByClient(pendingIssued[0]) });
  console.log(`  control (user approval): approval requests: ${describe(pendingIssued)}; after the user approves => ${approved.error ?? 'accepted'}; executed ${JSON.stringify(control.executed)}`);
}
```

